      <title>Foresight Linux: a new paradigm in distro making</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;o &amp;#39;traditionally&amp;#39; there were no &amp;#39;binary based&amp;#39; rolling            distributions,  for a reason.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;           The  idea is to show  how that is - with the right tools -&#xA;           not only possible, but in fact can change completely what to&#xA;           expect from a linux distribution.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;           The point is not to do a conary/rMake/foresight infomercial,&#xA;           but to present a new paradigm in distro making (Foresight&#xA;           Linux 2&#xA;           (expected H1/2008)), the challenges we face(d), etc.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;o Foresight Linux is a next generation linux distribution&#xA;           built around conary and rMake.&#xA;         o Currently released version (1.x train) has a very strong&#xA;           Gnome focus, and next version will have KDE and XFCE&#xA;           editions too.&#xA;         o Used as the base of the Official Gnome Development Kit.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
